Let bsd_init narrate itself

bsd_init_kprintf is compiled to boot_progress_stage while DEBUG_BSDINIT is 0,
and boot_progress_stage feeds the progress bar's buffer, not the console.  So
the forty-odd steps of bsd_init -- dev_kmem_init, kauth_init, vfsinit, mbinit,
socketinit, domaininit, skywalk_init, memorystatus_init, bsd_autoconf,
loopattach, ether_family_init, net_init_run, inittodr, setconf -- and above
all vfs_mountroot are invisible, and any claim about how far bsd_init got is
guesswork.

Turn the flag on: every step becomes one kprintf line, prefixed bsd_init:.
vfs_mountroot is the line that separates "still inside bsd_init" from
"handing the root volume to apfs".

---

diff --git a/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c b/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c
--- a/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c
@@ -495,7 +495,7 @@ bsd_init(void)
 	platform_stall_panic_or_spin(PLATFORM_STALL_XNU_LOCATION_BSD_INIT);
 #endif
 
-#define DEBUG_BSDINIT 0
+#define DEBUG_BSDINIT 1
 
 #if DEBUG_BSDINIT
 #define bsd_init_kprintf(x, ...) kprintf("bsd_init: " x, ## __VA_ARGS__)
